// car/cdr take a pair, and nil is not one (issue #236): (car nil) used to
// silently evaluate to nil, so `if car(x) == 1` quietly took the else branch
// whenever x was nil. The typechecker now rejects the arguments it can prove
// are nil — the literal form, and values whose type resolved to the nil base
// (net.close is declared `int -> nil`). Nils that only appear at runtime die
// with 'cartype/'cdrtype instead; see test/crash/car-cdr-nil-crash.ta.
// This file must be rejected by the typechecker.
// expect: cannot unify nil with pair
fn main() {
  car(nil)
  cdr(nil)
  car(net.close(0))
}